# -*- sh -*-
# VA-API driver for the Broadwell HD 5300 on MacBook8,1.
# Installed to /etc/X11/Xsession.d/56mintbook-libva. See docs/display.md.
#
# This file is sourced by Xsession(5), not executed.
#
# The same variable is also in /etc/environment.d/90-mintbook-libva.conf, and
# that file alone does not work. environment.d is read by `systemd --user`, and
# only reaches processes systemd itself starts. The desktop does not come from
# systemd: lightdm runs Xsession, Xsession starts xfce4-session, and everything
# launched from the panel, the dock or Whisker inherits *that* environment.
# Apps that land in a systemd *scope* (Chrome does) do not help either — a
# scope adopts a process that was already forked by the session, so it keeps
# the session's environment, not the manager's.
#
# Measured 2026-09-04: Cursor's /proc/<pid>/environ had GTK_MODULES, which ships
# in both /etc/X11/Xsession.d/90atk-adaptor and /etc/environment.d, but no
# LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME, which shipped only in environment.d. Same session, same
# two mechanisms, and only the Xsession.d one arrived. Chrome, Cursor and
# Claude Desktop all had iHD_drv_video mapped.
#
# Left unset so a value in ~/.xsessionrc (sourced earlier, at 40) still wins.
# 95dbus_update-activation-env runs after this and pushes the whole environment
# into dbus-daemon and systemd --user, so nothing else is needed here.
#
# Undo: delete this file and log out.
if [ -z "$LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME" ]; then
  LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME=i965
  export LIBVA_DRIVER_NAME
fi
